    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T05:51:37Z",
    "body": "> Any chance you'd be willing to redo this with a variable of sorts instead? This seems like a very fragile setup.\r\n\r\nYeah, I just hadn’t thought about it enough to realize how to make it not fragile\r\n\r\n> I was hoping for a _dataDragStoreWasChanged_ thingie since that's what you'd likely write in code too.\r\n\r\nOK, 2381a26 changes it to set and use an internal flag with that name\r\n\r\n>  just using our usual labeled steps style of `<i>Step label</i>: ...` then \"in the step labeled `<i>Step label</i>` would do the trick I think\r\n\r\nI could (re)change it to that if there’s a better reason to do it that way rather than setting an internal flag. But it seems like the labeled-step style is more for cases where we need to have the control flow in an algorithm jump back to a specific step?\r\n\r\n",
